 ## [9.0.1] — 2026-08-04
 
 ### Added
-- **Backup activation nudge** (`gsStorage.js`, `gsBackup.js`, `background.js`, `popup.html`, `popup.js`, `backup.html`, `backup.js`, `en/messages.json`, `it/messages.json`): users who have never enabled automatic backup (`AUTO_BACKUP_ENABLED = false`, the default) now see a quiet amber badge on the extension icon plus a banner in the popup and a note on the backup page, encouraging them to turn it on — prompted by issue #410, where a Chrome-side "corrupted extension" repair flow wiped a user's sessions with no backup in place. Users can snooze the nudge for 10 days (`BACKUP_NUDGE_DISMISSED_UNTIL`) or permanently opt out via a checkbox on the backup page (`BACKUP_NUDGE_OPTOUT`); there is no repeated popup/alert, only the persistent badge/banner/note.
-- **On-demand `downloads`/`identity` permissions and backup transparency** (`manifest.json`, `gsStorage.js`, `gsBackup.js`, `gsNewsFeed.js`, `backup.html`, `backup.js`, `options.html`, `options.js`, `en/messages.json`, `it/messages.json`): responding to issue #411, `downloads` and `identity` moved from unconditional `permissions` to `optional_permissions` — Chrome now only prompts for them when a user actually enables local backup (`chrome.permissions.request({permissions:['downloads']})` on the auto-backup checkbox) or connects Google Drive (`identity`, on the "Connetti Drive" button). Users who already had these granted under 9.0.0 see no re-prompt (`chrome.permissions.request` is a silent no-op when already granted, and Chrome preserves already-granted permissions across a required→optional manifest change). Also added: an opt-out for the daily news-feed request (`gsNewsFeedEnabled`, default on), a one-time in-app banner plus a persistent reference note pointing to the permissions documentation (`options.html`/`backup.html`), and a note explaining (plus automatic cleanup of) the local safety-net file `performEmergencyBackup` still writes when the configured destination is Drive-only.
